+PATCHED 15.4 — 05/10/2026
+Comment mode asks /api/v1/users/{id}/info/, the request every other mode already
+uses. Implementation complete, NOT validated against a real Instagram response
+(the build environment has no access to instagram.com or to the user's session).
+- Cause of 15.3: Comment mode asked web_profile_info, whose email field
+  data.user.business_email is null in every real capture kept; the public email
+  lives in user.public_email of /users/{id}/info/. The user authorised that route
+  for Comment mode.
+- One shared request: Comment calls the same function as the other modes
+  (ApiUserInfoDetail URL, the session's own headers, withCredentials). The reader
+  no longer builds a request; it only decides what the answer means. The
+  web_profile_info step is gone from the email flow: comment -> user_id ->
+  /users/{id}/info/ (half the requests).
+- Parser: the user object is located only in user, data.user or items[0].user
+  (checked against the requested id); email from public_email, else a filled
+  business_email; never bio, caption, comment, site, login or recovery data; CALL/TEXT
+  proves nothing.
+- States: email_found, no_public_email (HTTP 200 with the real profile only),
+  rate_limited (429), login_required (401, login/challenge, login page),
+  access_denied (403), temporary_error (network, 5xx, invalid answer), pending,
+  and profile_unavailable for a deleted profile (404). Failures are never saved as
+  results and never read as "no email". A profile without email, CALL/TEXT or
+  several empty answers in a row never stop the queue.
+- Persistent queue: rows are saved after every comment page together with the list
+  cursor (extract_queue_<history>); a resume continues exactly there, without
+  re-reading pages or repeating answered profiles. Rows answered by the old web
+  route without an email are asked again; rows that already hold an email are kept.
+  A comment without user.pk takes its id from user.pk_id/user.id/user_id or from a
+  saved answer, else it is keyed by username and never costs a request.
+- Persistent cache by user id (14 days with email, 7 without, 3 unavailable, 3000
+  entries), username -> id index from the same cache, cached rows skip the wait.
+- Pacing: Comment uses the same 15-30 s default as the other modes (saved range
+  wins, 10 s floor); a 429/400 doubles the spacing up to 2 min; five answers in a
+  row reduce it by 20%. One request at a time across dashboards.
+- Validation: the first real answer of a run shows a card (endpoint, HTTP, time,
+  public_email type, field path, Retry-After, parser decision, masked email);
+  "Validar 1 perfil pendente" does one request for the first pending profile and
+  leaves the answer saved for the queue; a 429 there stops everything.
+- Unchanged: 429 handling and the saved pause (same key, kept across the update),
+  Retry-After, no automatic retry, manifest key and extension id, permissions.
+
 PATCHED 15.3 — 05/10/2026
